name 'building-data-driven-systems-preassessment-q1_2025'

question 'A developer needs to store a list of 50 different song titles for a music app. Which data structure is the most efficient choice?'

wrong 'A single string containing all 50 titles separated by commas.'
wrong 'Fifty individual variables, each named after a different song.'
right 'An array, which allows all titles to be stored and accessed under one name.'
wrong 'A boolean variable that tracks if the playlist is currently playing.'

allow_multiple_attempts false

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 1

An array is specifically designed to store collections of related data. Storing them in a single string makes it hard to access individual items, and 50 variables would be impossible to manage at scale.
MARKDOWN
